            <ArticleTitle>Tryptase inhibitors - review of the recent patent literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>682-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The past several years has seen research increasingly focused around the inhibition of tryptase, a mast cell protease implicated in a myriad of pro-inflammatory responses. Although few compounds have reached the clinic, several monobasic and multibasic small molecules have emerged as promising candidates as a treatment for asthma and other allergic and inflammatory disorders. This summary reviews recent patent activity of tryptase inhibitors and briefly outlines recent tryptase inhibitor literature and clinical updates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
